WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:01.472
- [Kelly] I love it, I love it.

00:00:01.472 --> 00:00:03.101
So, we're just as "Destiny's Child",

00:00:03.101 --> 00:00:04.480
I feel like we're the same age.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.313
- [Elisabeth] Yeah.

00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:06.421
- So, did you, were you
a "Destiny's Child" fan?

00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:07.821
Of course.
- I know, right?

00:00:07.821 --> 00:00:08.780
- Of course, all of it.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:09.891
- I mean like way back, I'm like,

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:11.171
"Bug-A-Boo" days, like way...

00:00:11.171 --> 00:00:12.280
- Oh, yes.
- Yes.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.411
- Oh, yes.
- Yes.

00:00:13.411 --> 00:00:14.789
- Big, big, big, big.

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:16.781
- Yeah and I'm like,
"They have to have like,

00:00:16.781 --> 00:00:19.020
seven sets of lungs with that song".

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:19.989
There's nowhere to breathe.

00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:21.501
That was like, that's not fun.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.189
What was your first album, like purchased?

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.821
- Oh, you'll like this.
- What?

00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:25.654
- Paula Abdul.

00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:26.487
(Kelly gasps)
- Paula Abdul?

00:00:26.487 --> 00:00:27.420
- Yeah.
- I had...

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.253
- An old friend.

00:00:28.253 --> 00:00:29.712
- You'll like this, I
had that on cassette.

00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:30.545
- Oh, me too.

00:00:30.545 --> 00:00:31.378
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:32.211
- [Kelly] It was black.

00:00:32.211 --> 00:00:33.044
- I think we are like the same age.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:33.877
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:34.710
I'm 40.
- 40.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.729
- Oh, boom, oh.

00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:37.090
- '82 baby?
- Yes.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.210
- Boom.
- '82.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.256
- Yeah, it was a good year.

00:00:39.256 --> 00:00:40.089
- It was a very good year.

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:41.484
- It was a good year, no, that's amazing,

00:00:41.484 --> 00:00:42.694
that was one of my firsts, yeah.

00:00:42.694 --> 00:00:45.266
- Uh-huh, I had the
cassette and wore it out.

00:00:45.266 --> 00:00:46.099
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:00:46.099 --> 00:00:48.912
- Oh, my God, I was just
the biggest fan of hers.

00:00:48.912 --> 00:00:52.557
I mean, still am, but that
was just revolutionary for me.

00:00:52.557 --> 00:00:55.466
And I thought it was so, sort
of like naughty and sassy.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:56.299
- Of course.

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:57.505
- Remember like, "Cold Hearted Snake".

00:00:57.505 --> 00:00:59.816
- Yeah, she was on, on
that video, yes, yes.

00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:01.776
- That video, I was like, "Ooh".

00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:03.426
And now, when you watch it, it's like...

00:01:03.426 --> 00:01:04.866
- Now it's like...
- Nothing.

00:01:04.866 --> 00:01:06.376
- So, nothing compared
to what you see now.

00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:07.209
(Kelly and Elisabeth laugh)
Yeah, of course.

00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:08.175
But you know what's even better?

00:01:08.175 --> 00:01:10.422
Is I just remembered,
tapes, like cassettes.

00:01:10.422 --> 00:01:12.781
My children will never
know what rewind is.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.552
- Oh, yeah, they won't.

00:01:14.552 --> 00:01:15.385
- Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:15.385 --> 00:01:16.218
Like pressing rewind.

00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:17.051
That just hit me, I'm like,

00:01:17.051 --> 00:01:18.402
"Now you just go back
to where you wanna go".

00:01:18.402 --> 00:01:19.660
You know what I'm saying?
You drag it or something.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.518
- Yeah, if you got lost in
the middle of like a side,

00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:23.890
you would've had to go
back and like two songs.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.668
- [Kelly] Rewind, fast
forward, rewind, fast forward.

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:26.501
- It was a journey.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:27.520
- [Kelly] Yes, it was a journey.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.850
Anyway, I just thought of that.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.130
Was anyone in your family musical?

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.661
- Yeah, everyone actually,
no one was in acting

00:01:33.661 --> 00:01:34.869
or film or TV or anything.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:36.720
Everyone was in the
music business with jazz,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.553
jazz and blues.

00:01:37.553 --> 00:01:39.040
- Oh, that's intense, okay.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.720
- I know, so, everyone played instruments.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.553
- [Kelly] They're like great musicians.

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:42.386
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:43.219
- [Kelly] If they're playing jazz, yeah.

00:01:43.219 --> 00:01:44.829
- Real, real, yeah, real musicians, yeah.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:46.386
- Well, I heard that you shared
a room with your brother.

00:01:46.386 --> 00:01:47.219
- [Elisabeth] Yeah, of course.

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:48.677
- Was that fun since he played music?

00:01:48.677 --> 00:01:49.906
Was it...
(Kelly and Elisabeth laugh)

00:01:49.906 --> 00:01:50.739
- Good question.

00:01:50.739 --> 00:01:51.922
(Kelly chuckles)

00:01:51.922 --> 00:01:53.645
I mean, my brother and I are really close.

00:01:53.645 --> 00:01:54.506
I love him very much.

00:01:54.506 --> 00:01:56.365
So, now I'm nostalgic for the days

00:01:56.365 --> 00:01:58.306
that I shared like a room with him.

00:01:58.306 --> 00:02:00.885
At the time though, of course,
he was my little brother

00:02:00.885 --> 00:02:02.893
and he loved to talk and was very chatty.

00:02:02.893 --> 00:02:04.596
So, he would sort of keep
me up all night talking,

00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:07.767
which now I'm like, "Oh, I miss that".

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:10.215
But of course at the time, you
know, he kept me all night.

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:11.143
- Yeah and you're like, "Just shut up".

00:02:11.143 --> 00:02:12.436
- And then he got a drum set.

00:02:12.436 --> 00:02:13.326
- [Kelly] And then he got a drum set?

00:02:13.326 --> 00:02:14.484
- And then he got another drum set.

00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:15.317
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:16.150
Multiple drum sets.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:16.983
And that's when he moved downstairs.

00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:18.545
- [Kelly] Oh, that's amazing.

00:02:18.545 --> 00:02:19.697
- Underneath my room.

00:02:19.697 --> 00:02:21.737
- Oh, that's not so great, that's not,

00:02:21.737 --> 00:02:23.756
so, you constantly have the
heartbeat of your brother.

00:02:23.756 --> 00:02:25.606
- Exactly, so we got him
the, like electrical drums

00:02:25.606 --> 00:02:26.665
with the headphones.
- Oh, with the headphones.

00:02:26.665 --> 00:02:27.498
Yes.

00:02:27.498 --> 00:02:29.617
- So, it was better, but you
could still hear the like...

00:02:29.617 --> 00:02:31.257
(Elisabeth taps)

00:02:31.257 --> 00:02:32.264
You know?
- Oh, man.

00:02:32.264 --> 00:02:34.441
My poor mom, I played violin.

00:02:34.441 --> 00:02:35.274
- Oh, God.

00:02:35.274 --> 00:02:36.865
- And not well.
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:39.236
Like it was, she was a trooper.

00:02:39.236 --> 00:02:40.069
- [Elisabeth] That is brave.

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:42.324
But it was, yeah, it was brave of me.

00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:43.745
You grew up in L.A, so...
- Yeah.

00:02:43.745 --> 00:02:46.252
- Did doing things like
going to Disneyland,

00:02:46.252 --> 00:02:47.205
because I lived in Orange County

00:02:47.205 --> 00:02:48.396
for a little bit when I was a kid.

00:02:48.396 --> 00:02:49.229
- [Elisabeth] Oh, you did?

00:02:49.229 --> 00:02:50.364
- Yeah, like right by Disneyland.

00:02:50.364 --> 00:02:51.932
I thought it was so cool
and we went all the time.

00:02:51.932 --> 00:02:52.943
- We went all the time.
- Yeah.

00:02:52.943 --> 00:02:53.991
- We did not live in Orange County,

00:02:53.991 --> 00:02:56.162
we lived in Royal Canyon,
but we went all the time.

00:02:56.162 --> 00:02:57.028
It was like 40 minutes away.

00:02:57.028 --> 00:02:57.861
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:57.861 --> 00:02:59.122
- Multiple times a year.

00:02:59.122 --> 00:03:01.343
- [Kelly] I'm still like a
grownup that loves to go.

00:03:01.343 --> 00:03:02.471
- Are you kidding? It's
like my favorite place.

00:03:02.471 --> 00:03:03.304
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:03:03.304 --> 00:03:04.463
- Yeah, like my children get excited

00:03:04.463 --> 00:03:05.742
and then there's my excitement.

00:03:05.742 --> 00:03:06.612
(Elisabeth chuckles)
Yeah.

00:03:06.612 --> 00:03:09.789
- I haven't been since the
whole pandemic thing, obviously,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.922
but I used to go every year.

00:03:11.922 --> 00:03:12.755
I used to go every year.

00:03:12.755 --> 00:03:14.743
And recently in the past like few years,

00:03:14.743 --> 00:03:17.391
I discovered that you could get a guide.

00:03:17.391 --> 00:03:20.002
So, if you like pool,
a bunch of friends...

00:03:20.002 --> 00:03:21.702
- Life changing.

00:03:21.702 --> 00:03:23.452
- Game changer.
- Yes.

00:03:23.452 --> 00:03:24.285
- So, it's not like cheap,

00:03:24.285 --> 00:03:26.423
but if you get like,
five, six, seven people

00:03:26.423 --> 00:03:29.183
and you all pool your money,
like you can get this guide.

00:03:29.183 --> 00:03:30.016
- Yes.

00:03:30.016 --> 00:03:32.002
- [Elisabeth] Who basically,
like gets you through the lines

00:03:32.002 --> 00:03:34.381
and what's great is you
focus on their rides.

00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:36.559
You get on more rides,
which is the objective.

00:03:36.559 --> 00:03:39.109
- Yes, but so, what's not great though,

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:41.248
is that you go, this is
a first world problem,

00:03:41.248 --> 00:03:43.609
but they put you on the ride so fast.

00:03:43.609 --> 00:03:44.442
- [Elisabeth] Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:44.442 --> 00:03:47.219
- That your body never has the hour or two

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:49.140
that you're usually waiting in the lines.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:49.973
- [Elisabeth] Yes, so like...

00:03:49.973 --> 00:03:51.267
- So, your body, so then all
of a sudden you're like...

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.100
(Kelly groans)

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.527
Like, like, you know,
you're about to barf.

00:03:53.527 --> 00:03:54.360
(Elisabeth laughs)

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.478
- I used to be able to ride Space Mountain

00:03:55.478 --> 00:03:57.239
like, multiple times in a row.

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.198
- [Kelly] Tops, two for me.

00:03:58.198 --> 00:04:00.018
- And now I'm like, "I
don't think I'm good".

00:04:00.018 --> 00:04:01.096
- Yeah.
- I don't think I'm good.

00:04:01.096 --> 00:04:02.388
- And I have to like, I'm so old,

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:03.988
I have to like planned food around like,

00:04:03.988 --> 00:04:04.901
when I can ride or not ride.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:05.734
(Kelly and Elisabeth chuckle)
- Yeah.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:06.892
- I'm like, "It'll come back up".

00:04:06.892 --> 00:04:07.795
- Absolutely, absolutely.

00:04:07.795 --> 00:04:08.964
- [Kelly] Well, that's a great age.

00:04:08.964 --> 00:04:09.797
(audience applauds)

00:04:09.797 --> 00:04:11.822
That was a look at season
five of "The Handmaid's Tale".

00:04:11.822 --> 00:04:13.905
You can see it now on Hulu.

00:04:13.905 --> 00:04:15.696
The show, for those who don't know,

00:04:15.696 --> 00:04:18.355
is about a dystopian world
in which the United States

00:04:18.355 --> 00:04:21.473
has split forming a country called Gilead,

00:04:21.473 --> 00:04:24.705
in which citizens are forced
to play specific roles.

00:04:24.705 --> 00:04:27.075
So, your character, June

00:04:27.075 --> 00:04:29.086
has escaped Gilead like four times.

00:04:29.086 --> 00:04:31.646
So, where do we find her this season?

00:04:31.646 --> 00:04:33.825
- I am not in Gilead.
- Okay.

00:04:33.825 --> 00:04:36.825
- At the top of the
season, I am in Canada.

00:04:36.825 --> 00:04:39.097
She's trying to kind of recover

00:04:39.097 --> 00:04:42.235
from the terrible sort of murder that her

00:04:42.235 --> 00:04:44.065
and her friends committed
at the end of last season.

00:04:44.065 --> 00:04:44.898
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:44.898 --> 00:04:46.915
- I like bringing these
stories to your daytime show.

00:04:46.915 --> 00:04:49.105
- Yeah, we just like to cheer
people up here, Elisabeth.

00:04:49.105 --> 00:04:50.265
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:50.265 --> 00:04:53.048
- Afternoon.
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:53.048 --> 00:04:54.286
So, she's recovering from that

00:04:54.286 --> 00:04:56.473
and she's also trying to figure out

00:04:56.473 --> 00:05:00.795
how to be a mother and a
wife and a human and a woman.

00:05:00.795 --> 00:05:04.363
And also, be somebody who has
gone through extreme trauma.

00:05:04.363 --> 00:05:06.926
- So, like a lot of people
now, like that's, yeah,

00:05:06.926 --> 00:05:08.534
that's a very relatable thing, so...

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:09.585
- [Elisabeth] It can be, very much so.

00:05:09.585 --> 00:05:10.418
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:10.418 --> 00:05:13.555
- So, what perspective
has the series given you

00:05:13.555 --> 00:05:14.835
on what's been going on with women

00:05:14.835 --> 00:05:16.305
and women's rights and
everything right now?

00:05:16.305 --> 00:05:18.105
I mean...
- Because it's kind of eerie.

00:05:18.105 --> 00:05:19.995
- Yeah, I liked your documentary.

00:05:19.995 --> 00:05:20.828
(Kelly chuckles)

00:05:20.828 --> 00:05:22.566
- [Kelly] That was, that
was Jordan, our writer.

00:05:22.566 --> 00:05:23.585
It was very funny.

00:05:23.585 --> 00:05:25.134
- It was good.
- Yeah.

00:05:25.134 --> 00:05:28.694
- You know, I mean as
a human and as a woman

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:31.734
and a citizen, of course,
I have my own feelings

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:34.385
and my own, you know,
what I think is right

00:05:34.385 --> 00:05:35.494
and what I think is wrong.

00:05:35.494 --> 00:05:36.327
- Yeah.

00:05:36.327 --> 00:05:37.795
- When you're a part of a show like that,

00:05:37.795 --> 00:05:40.014
of course you get so much more of it

00:05:40.014 --> 00:05:41.705
and it's a part of your everyday life.

00:05:41.705 --> 00:05:43.174
And you're living out these scenarios.

00:05:43.174 --> 00:05:44.075
- [Kelly] You're faced with it.

00:05:44.075 --> 00:05:45.603
- You're faced with it every day

00:05:45.603 --> 00:05:48.315
and you're having conversations
every day about it,

00:05:48.315 --> 00:05:49.534
in a, in a really deep way,

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.143
which I have found very fulfilling

00:05:51.143 --> 00:05:53.534
and I have found very eye
opening and very educating,

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.375
because now a lot of people come to me,

00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:56.785
a lot of people share things with me.

00:05:56.785 --> 00:05:59.473
I hear people's stories
and from all over the world

00:05:59.473 --> 00:06:03.555
and it's, it's been a very
gratifying experience as a woman.

00:06:03.555 --> 00:06:05.195
- Yeah, I love the direct impact.

00:06:05.195 --> 00:06:06.385
I think that that's when people do learn

00:06:06.385 --> 00:06:09.035
and progress, is you have
some kind of direct impact

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:12.475
to whatever that cause is or
whatever thing is happening.

00:06:12.475 --> 00:06:13.308
- [Elisabeth] Yeah.

00:06:13.308 --> 00:06:14.141
- And I think that's important.

00:06:14.141 --> 00:06:15.121
- It is and you know, we're telling...

00:06:15.121 --> 00:06:16.905
- That's why I think this
kind of series is important.

00:06:16.905 --> 00:06:17.738
- Thank you, thank you.

00:06:17.738 --> 00:06:19.943
Yeah, you know, we're telling
our story through one lens.

00:06:19.943 --> 00:06:21.225
We're telling it through June's lens.

00:06:21.225 --> 00:06:22.323
It's called, "The Handmaid's Tale".

00:06:22.323 --> 00:06:25.755
It's her story, but I hope,
and what has happened,

00:06:25.755 --> 00:06:27.385
I hope continues to happen,

00:06:27.385 --> 00:06:30.094
is it does continue to open up the space

00:06:30.094 --> 00:06:32.214
for other people to share their stories,

00:06:32.214 --> 00:06:33.705
whether they're similar or not.

00:06:33.705 --> 00:06:35.813
And other people from other
walks of life and other...

00:06:35.813 --> 00:06:36.646
- [Kelly] Other perspectives.

00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:38.203
- Exactly, other perspectives.

00:06:38.203 --> 00:06:41.563
And I, I really enjoy and
value that conversation.

00:06:41.563 --> 00:06:43.144
- I do too, I love conversation.

00:06:43.144 --> 00:06:45.814
Especially, I love being at a
table when people don't agree.

00:06:45.814 --> 00:06:46.647
[Elisabeth] Yes.

00:06:46.647 --> 00:06:48.385
- Because I find that exciting,
because you learn something.

00:06:48.385 --> 00:06:49.218
- [Elisabeth] Absolutely.

00:06:49.218 --> 00:06:50.774
- And it, and it, it just,

00:06:50.774 --> 00:06:52.403
I love those kind of conversations.

00:06:52.403 --> 00:06:54.195
Most people don't, but I do,

00:06:54.195 --> 00:06:55.425
or most people I'm around don't.

00:06:55.425 --> 00:06:56.258
- Yeah.

00:06:56.258 --> 00:06:57.574
- But I, but I do, I love it.

00:06:57.574 --> 00:06:58.915
I genuinely get excited about it.

00:06:58.915 --> 00:06:59.853
- That's how you learn.

00:06:59.853 --> 00:07:01.633
- So, you are, I, I love this.

00:07:01.633 --> 00:07:02.843
You're directing again.
- Yeah.

00:07:02.843 --> 00:07:03.933
I think that's exciting.

00:07:03.933 --> 00:07:04.766
- [Elisabeth] Thank you.
(audience applauds)

00:07:04.766 --> 00:07:06.465
- Not every actor wants
to do all the things

00:07:06.465 --> 00:07:07.654
and I think that's really cool,

00:07:07.654 --> 00:07:09.142
that you love like, challenging yourself.

00:07:09.142 --> 00:07:11.163
So, what's it like directing?

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:13.471
Bradley, like y'all worked
together on "West Wing",

00:07:13.471 --> 00:07:15.061
so, is that weird?

00:07:15.061 --> 00:07:16.593
Because you were very
young on "West Wing".

00:07:16.593 --> 00:07:18.054
- [Elisabeth] Yeah, I
was 17 when I met him

00:07:18.054 --> 00:07:20.662
and he was my age when he met me.

00:07:20.662 --> 00:07:21.495
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

